  "summary": "Arsenal recovered from a goal down to beat Leeds 2–1 at the Emirates on Saturday 10 October. Sky Sports reports that Riccardo Calafiori equalised before substitute Bruno Guimaraes struck the winner in the 70th minute. The result ended Leeds’ unbeaten league start and brought Arsenal level on points with Manchester City ahead of City’s visit to Liverpool.",
